        "id": 33972,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-07-07T12:33:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Whispers from the … er … sidelines?!</p>\n<p>The con has been great! I haven’t actually played Sentinels yet – that will be today and tomorrow – but I went by last night to scope it out. The dealer hall is puny compared to GenCon or Origins,<br>\nbut still quite sizeable – there were a couple dozen booths and some great stuff. I may need to buy a chainmail dice pouch and I’m a huge Doctor 11/Amy Pond fan so there’s a book about Series 5 that I might need to buy, too.</p>\n<p>There are a couple of game rooms, one of which is dedicated to board games. There’s a library where one can check out games. Again it’s puny compared to what was available at GenCon or Origins, but it’s really quite good. There are no tables assigned in advance, so for those people who are running games, you just check in with the people managing the room and work with them to pick out a space.</p>\n<p>I <em>finally</em> joined my friend Chris to hear the band he’s been raving about – 5 Year Mission. They are a local Indy band that has decided to do an original song based on each of the episodes in Star Trek the original series. It was pretty awesome. During the songs they play clips from the related episode. <a href=\"http://fiveyearmission.net/\">http://fiveyearmission.net/</a></p>\n<p>I topped off the evening by sitting in on the Filk circle, which was totally awesome. Not only was there some really great music, but it was a very welcoming group of people.</p>\n<p>I have little idea how many people will come by to play today and/or whether I’ll run demos or full games. It’s an adventure!</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
