        "id": 33976,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-07-08T13:15:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Too tired last night to post.</p>\n<p>I ran the game from 10am to 2pm yesterday, Traffic was light, but there were enough people interested that I was playing the game most of the time. Some experienced players came by so I felt comfortable breaking out not only my personal copy of Rook City but also some of the playtest decks. It was great fun and hopefully some of the cool people will come and join us at the regular meetups.</p>\n<p>Observation: Loving the game and playing a lot does not necessarily mean that I’m particularly good at it. We got our butts handed to us by Plague Rat. Also, playing demos where the villain’s hit points are set artificially low can give me bad habits – like it hardly matters what I do, we’re still going to win. Also, STOP GIVING YOURSELF BUFFS WHEN PLAYING AGAINST PLAGUE RAT! Yeesh. I was playing Mr. Fixer and buffed him up in anticipation of getting the style that allowed him to redirect, but never got it.</p>\n<p>And then the con became all about music! There’s a local Indianapolis Filk/Rock band (Wild Mercy: <a href=\"http://www.wildmercy.com/\">http://www.wildmercy.com/</a>) who were the musical guests of honor. I spent most of the rest of the day Sat seeing them and a number of other groups.</p>",
